CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ operator D\(\) then D->B slicing works: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [over.match.copy]/1: a source conversion function yielding a class derived
from the target type is a candidate when converting to that class type (then
derived-to-base initialization).  CBMC previously rejected S::operator D() when
converting to base B (CONVERSION ERROR) because user_defined_conversion_sequence
required standard_conversion_sequence(operator-result, T), which does not model
the derived-to-base initialization of a class prvalue.  Fixed by converting the
operator result to the target base via address-of + pointer derived-to-base +
dereference.  Non-vacuous: assertion 2 must FAIL.
